description:
Ref No. JD-082 R1
Candidate shall be assigned to oversee an internationally based integrated consultancy and advisory team.

Company:
Alpin Limited is a leading sustainability consultant in the Middle East, with its global headquarters in Masdar City, Abu Dhabi—the world's first sustainable city. We're on a mission to transform the built environment by providing innovative commissioning, sustainability, and climate change solutions. As a company, we are committed to thought leadership and making a tangible difference in the world. We pride ourselves on having a diverse, multicultural team of experts who are passionate about creating a more sustainable future. At Alpin, you'll be part of a dynamic, "young-at-heart" culture that values collaboration, innovation, and continuous learning.
To know more about Alpin Limited and its services and projects please visit www.alpinme.com

Reports Directly to :
Head of Sustainability/Acting Head of Sustainability

Roles and Responsibilities:
• Shall be responsible for stakeholder engagement and satisfaction (internal and external), project delivery performance, QA/QC, timely invoicing, team leadership/mentorship, and BD/contract support;
• Shall be responsible for implementing the Individual roles and responsibilities matrix issued by the Head of Department;
• Shall be responsible for project governance and reporting to the Sustainability HoD, including communication plans, reporting cadence, and monthly progress reporting in the agreed format;
• Shall be responsible for stakeholder mapping and management across assigned projects and accounts;
• Shall be responsible for establishing and managing project meeting schedules and coordination cadence with consultants and internal teams;
• Shall be responsible for delivery controls across assigned projects, including programme milestone adherence, timely deliverables, and closure of review comments within agreed timeframes;
• Shall be responsible for QA/QC execution, including internal technical reviews prior to client issue, document control compliance, and use of approved templates, tools and checklists;
• Shall be responsible for commercial discipline, including fee burn tracking, scope/change control support, and early warning/escalation of commercial risk to the HoD;
• Shall be responsible for risk and issue management, including early identification, escalation, and tracking of mitigation actions to closure;
• Shall be responsible for client relationship management, including structured feedback capture and actioning improvement items;
• Shall be responsible for day-to-day delivery coordination with the Senior Operations Manager, including planning, priorities, resourcing requests and task tracking;
• Shall be responsible for technical oversight of sustainability deliverables, including (as applicable) certification strategies, carbon and life-cycle deliverables, climate resilience inputs, and aligned sustainability narratives;
• Shall be responsible for team capability development, including technical guidance, training, lessons learned, and knowledge sharing as directed by the HoD.
HSE Roles, Responsibilities and Accountability:
· The Managing HoD’s HSE role is to support ensure all Employees are aware of the Company’s HSE Policy.
· Responsibility: As defined in IMS_01, Clase 5.5.1 “Responsibility and Authority”
· Accountability: Accountable for ensuring the right resources are allocated for the proper implementation and functioning of the Company’s Integrated Management System.

Skills:
• Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in a technically related discipline (Environmental, Construction Management, Engineering or Architecture) plus MBA or equivalent professional experience;
• LEED AP and/or equivalent senior accreditation (e.g., BREEAM AP, WELL AP, Estidama PQP, MOSTADAM AP) aligned to service delivery;
• 10–15 years of industry experience (technical consulting, not necessarily in sustainability);
• Advanced knowledge of current sustainability standards: LEED, BREEAM, MOSTADAM, QSAS, or Estidama;
• GCC experience;
• Excellent written and spoken English (ability to understand contract language);
• Passport that allows travel within the GCC and European Union without restrictions;
• Knowledge of current sustainability standards: LEED, BREEAM, Green Star, QSAS, or Estidama;
• Proven experience leading and motivating teams, with strong facilitation, team building and collaboration skills;
• Advanced presentation and communication skills (clear, concise and effective);
• Experience in new business development and proposal support;
• Understanding of and experience with finance/accounting;
• Understanding of branding and marketing;
• High degree of professionalism and strong interpersonal skills, with ability to work with clients, consultants and other stakeholders;
• Demonstrated capability in delivery planning and tracking (programme, risks, actions, issues, deliverable registers) and QA/QC technical review processes for consultant deliverables
• Preferably an Arabic speaker

Department

Sustainability

Location

Riyadh, KSA

About Alpin Limited

As a young company full of creative energy and a passion for excellence, we are the perfect fit for an individual who strives to succeed and enjoys the challenge of working on cutting-edge international projects (not all project positions require travel). Follow us on LinkedIn , Facebook & Twitter .

Founded in

2007

At Waad Education Schools, we are seeking dedicated and experienced Administrative Professionals to join our growing school community.

The ideal candidates are organized, proactive team players who demonstrate strong communication skills, support daily operations effectively, build positive relationships with staff and parents, and collaborate closely with leadership to ensure a smooth and professional school environment.

If you are passionate about education and thrive in a dynamic workplace, we would love to hear from you.

**Requirements**

* Bachelor’s degree or higher in a relevant field.
* Minimum 3 years of administrative experience, preferably in an educational environment.
* Strong organizational, communication, and multitasking skills.
* Ability to work collaboratively within a school team.
* Professional certifications are a plus.

**Benefits**

* Opportunity to work in an inspiring environment with high focus on quality and holistic education;
* Supportive and collaborative colleagues;
* Clear mechanism and opportunities for long-term career growth;
* Continuous professional development;
* Health insurance;
* Fully paid vacation;
* Annual flights to home country;
* Scholarships for children as per company policy.

Eram Talent is a leading Talent Acquisition Consultancy focused on placing highly skilled professionals in various industries across the globe. We are currently seeking a Field Compliance Coordinator specializing in Drilling Safety and Environment for one of our prominent clients in the oil and gas sector. In this role, the Field Compliance Coordinator will ensure that safety and environmental regulations are adhered to in drilling operations, collaborating closely with field teams, contractors, and management to mitigate risks and promote a safe working environment.

**Functional Job Title: Drilling Field compliance coordinators (Safety and Environment)**

### JOB DESCRIPTION:

The successful candidate will be required to perform the following:

* Act as the UR Operations Excellence & Compliance Division Field HSE Advisor, EMS focal point, reports to Group Lead and maintains daily communications with assigned departments ops managers to provide key support, in regards of E&OH for field and office activities;
* Provide field support in regards of daily activities environmental impacts, environmental release events and E&OH audits/inspections;
* Review the annual environmental objectives and programs (action plans) proposed by UROE&CD with department management and signs off on department approved environmental objectives;
* Obtains monthly updates from department training coordinator to verify the department’s environmental/ EMS compliance and reports deficiencies, if any, to the group lead;
* Reviews and reports new (or changes in) departmental processes and/or procedures that may have an environmental impact (adverse or beneficial) and may affect achievement of desired EMS outcomes to UROE&CD;
* Conduct EMS assessments, E&OH inspections (ECAs, OHHAs, CEHAs, RPAs, NORM surveys and EH surveys) as per schedules;
* Produce the non-compliance reports and communicate them to unit supervisor;
* Monitors the performance of Environmental emergency drill scenarios and follows up with any identified deficiencies;
* Monitor and reports the department daily activities environmental data and performance indicators on Flaring, SO2, Greenhouse gas emissions (GHG), Water Conservation, Energy, etc; and
* Advice UR Operations on managing environmental risks and provide recommendations to mitigate impacts

**Requirements**

* The successful candidate should hold a Bachelor degree in, Engineering, HSE, Science, Industrial, or in a related discipline from an accredited entity or equivalent. A Master’s Degree in Environment is preferable.
* Minimum 10 years of experience in environmental compliance related to drilling and completion operations
* shall demonstrate/prove a high level of Environmental management skills with expertise in oil and gas or other related activities.
* Certified and/or have knowledge and field experience in Environmental management systems (preferably Internal/Lead audit certifications ISO 14001, other training certifications related to environmental sustainability, air mitigations, hazardous waste, GHG, water/wastewater management, NORM/ radioactive, spill control, noise control, and etc.)
* preferably to have demonstrated knowledge of delivering hands on environmental training and conducting of different environmental awareness sessions.
* preferably to have good knowledge of environmental concepts, international environmental standards, and industry related environmental standards, and research methods.
* Ability to write reports; ability to work with others and communicate technical concepts and ideas to non-technical personnel and the public; ability to read, write, speak, understand, and communicate in English sufficiently to perform the essential duties of the position; ability to use computer applications.

## How will you CONTRIBUTE and GROW?

The Large Industries Business Development (LIBD) works at the intersection of strategy, commercial, finance and project management activities. She/He drives the growth of the Large Industries business line by orchestrating the solution sales process of multi million investment projects. The LIBD fuses strategy development, customer relations, financial model, commercial offers and contract management.  

The successful candidate demonstrates an equilibrium of following skills: strategic thinking, clients and relationship management, oral and written communication, abstract and critical thinking, financial modeling, project management and problem solving. A knowledge of refining, chemical or petrochemical process or the energy transition considerations is a plus.

**1\. Business development**

* Establish, maintain and grow trustful relationship with large corporations in oil refining, chemical, petrochemical or steel industries;

* Identifies, understand and analyze the customers needs, process, projects and pain points;

* Explore the customer organizations, decision making criteria and leaders;

* Assess competitive moves, capabilities and contexts surrounding the sales leads;

* Ensure a good internal networking for awareness and alignment between departments and entities;

* Based on above:

    \- identifies / initiates  business growth opportunities aligned with company strategy

    \- elaborates the winning strategy and underlying solution, supported by qualitative and quantitative arguments;

    \- writes commercial presentations, offers and bids;

    \- writes, in collaboration with legal teams, and negotiates with customers, the project framework agreements: gas supply agreements, utilities agreements, memorandums, etc.


**2\. Project Development**

* Identifies and mobilizes the required resources to form ad-hoc cross-functional project teams including engineering, legal, finance and other departments;

* Defines the cost, scope and schedule of the assigned business growth opportunities to deliver winning solutions to customers and profitable growth to Large Industries;

* Ensures a timely and rigorous investment and decision making process internally and externally;

* Writes key internal project deliverables including investment committee notes;


**3\. Finance**

* Knows the basic principles and relationship between profit and loss, cash flow and balance sheet

* Understands the investment notions of time value of money, net present value, internal rate of return, hurdle rates and opportunity costs

* Calculates and accurately controls the project financial model for pricing and investment decision needs;


## \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_

## Are you a MATCH?

****Qualifications & Experience:** *(list education, certifications, training, work experience, etc.)***

* Bachelor's degree in relevant engineering or finance; MBA degree  is a plus.

* A minimum of 5 to 7 years of business development experience involving investment decisions.

* A knowledge of refining, chemical or petrochemical process or the energy transition considerations is a plus.



****Skills and Competencies:** *(list technical & core skills, soft skills, behavioral competencies, etc.)***

* Honest, credible, empathic personality capable to build trustful long term relationships;

* Ease of interaction across management lines, including senior management internal & external

* Strategic thinking and commercial spirit oriented on winning while delivering the value;

* Autonomous, entrepreneurial and self-driven personality;

* Strong critical thinking and analytical skills;

* Good organization and project management habits;

* Able to deliver structured and concise oral and written messages and documents;

* Ease and accuracy in financial modeling and other calculations;

* Ability to travel within the Middle East.


**Our Differences make our Performance**


At Air Liquide, we are committed to build a diverse and inclusive workplace that embraces the diversity of our employees, our customers, patients, community stakeholders and cultures across the world.  

We welcome and consider applications from all qualified applicants, regardless of their background. We strongly believe a diverse organization opens up opportunities for people to express their talent, both individually and collectively and it helps foster our ability to innovate by living our fundamentals, acting for our success and creating an engaging environment in a changing world.



A world leader in gases, technologies and services for Industry and Health.

Through the passion and diversity of its people, Air Liquide leverages energy and environment transition, changes in healthcare and digitization, and delivers greater value to all its stakeholders.

Join us for a stimulating experience: you’ll find a world of learning and development opportunities where inventiveness is at the heart of what we do, in an open, collaborative and respectful environment.

****Discover what your professional journey at Air Liquide could be** [here](https://www.airliquide.com/join-us/your-professional-journey)**!****



We want to ensure a safe experience for everyone interested in joining Air Liquide. Please be aware of fraudulent job offers that are circulating, falsely using the Air Liquide name and brand. These scams often involve individuals or organizations impersonating Air Liquide recruiters or employees through fake emails, social media, and websites. They may attempt to request personal information or, critically, ask for payment for various reasons like application fees, training, or visa processing. **Please be advised that Air Liquide and our authorized recruitment partners will never ask you for money at any stage of the recruitment process.**

You may verify job postings through our official global [careers website](https://airliquidehr.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/AirLiquideExternalCareer) at any time. If you receive a suspicious job offer or request for payment/sensitive data, we strongly advise that you do not respond or click on any links. We encourage you to verify the source carefully and only interact through our official channels. We appreciate your interest in Air Liquide and are committed to combating these fraudulent activities to protect job seekers. If you wish to report an incident, please contact us via this [form](https://www.airliquide.com/contact)

