Ref No. JD-135
The candidate shall be assigned to an integrated sustainability team for projects within the Middle East and Europe.

Company:
Alpin Limited is a leading sustainability consultant in the Middle East, with its global headquarters in Masdar City, Abu Dhabi—the world's first sustainable city. We're on a mission to transform the built environment by providing innovative commissioning, sustainability, and climate change solutions. As a company, we are committed to thought leadership and making a tangible difference in the world. We pride ourselves on having a diverse, multicultural team of experts who are passionate about creating a more sustainable future. At Alpin, you'll be part of a dynamic, "young-at-heart" culture that values collaboration, innovation, and continuous learning.
To know more about Alpin Limited and its services and projects please visit www.alpinme.com

Reports Directly to :
Head of Department - Sustainability and/or Team Leaders

Roles and Responsibilities:
· Member of Sustainability team;
· Participate as a team leader in carrying out specific global and local projects such as sustainable building projects, operational efficiency, etc.;
· Quality control and review of reports;
· Lead Presentations;
· Business Development Support;
· Support the company in its rapid growth plans;
· Understand and implement the principles of project management (scheduling, resource planning, effective meetings, stakeholder management);
· Site and Office Based Consultancy;
· Manage the green building design and LEED/Mostadam/WELL documentation process as well as project specifications, calculations, plans and submittals for LEED/Mostadam/WELL compliance;
· Coordinate with/support contractors including MEP and civil engineers;
· Conduct product and technology research related to sustainability;
· Contributions to regional publications, lectures, teaching assignments;
· Personal development and plan to develop skills necessary for promotion to Sr. Sustainability Consultant.

HSE Roles, Responsibilities and Accountability:
· In addition to your responsibility towards following ALPIN’s Integrated Management System, every employee at ALPIN is required to familiarize themselves with ALPIN’s Environmental Impact Assessment and contribute towards minimizing their individual environmental impact in the course of their work.
· It is the duty of all employees to act within the legal responsibilities imposed upon them and the Company’s Quality, Environment and Health & Safety policies. All employees must familiarize themselves with the Company’s Integrated Management System’s policies and procedures

Skills:
· Strong interpersonal skills and ability to work with both clients and consultants;
· Have a background within the built environment sector (3 - 5 years);
· Working Knowledge of MEP, Construction Management and Design;
· Demonstrated project experience;
· Strong Knowledge of current sustainability standards: LEED, Mostadam, and/or WELL;
· LEED AP is a must (commitment to achieve 2nd within 1 month); MOSTADAM AP, WELL AP or other certification as required to execute works
· Comprehensive written & spoken English;
· Bachelor’s Degree in related discipline (Environmental, Construction Management, Engineering or Architecture);
· GCC experience;
· Excellent planning and organization skills required for our fast-paced environment;
· Ability to self-manage;
· Strong communication skills (Written, electronic & spoken)

Additional Experience/Certifications:
· Hands-on engineering and project management skills;
· Arabic language would be a plus (not required);
· Master’s Degree is a plus (not required);
· Driver’s license is required & personal mode of transportation in country of hire (preferred);
· Passport which allows for efficient regional travel.

### Job Overview

Act as a Senior IT Engineer for the Saudi Arabia branch — the technical backbone of local IT delivery — owning local IT infrastructure, operations, security and compliance, and asset management end-to-end as an individual contributor, while serving as a key IT liaison between China HQ and the subsidiary. You will execute local IT strategy, ensure regulatory and information-security compliance, and drive global corporate IT standards adoption locally. **Minimum 5 years of progressive IT infrastructure and operations experience**; proven track record supporting IT compliance and security programs (e.g. audits, regulator liaison, ISO 27001 / SOC 2 / PCI DSS alignment) is required.

Key Responsibilities

1.  Implement corporate IT standards, policies and security requirements, align local infrastructure with global IT architecture, drive initiatives and ensure remediation closure; provide regular updates to HQ and local management, including incident escalation details and resolution status;
2.  Independently deliver IT infrastructure projects for offices and client-facing sites, including site survey, cabling planning, hardware deployment and system commissioning to complete full-cycle site rollout;
3.  Establish standardised PC endpoint framework, manage bulk deployment, ongoing support and troubleshooting of business applications;
4.  Maintain AV conferencing systems, access control, CCTV, IP telephony and multi-function printers;
5.  Administer DNS and DHCP network services, and independently resolve a wide range of network incidents;
6.  Manage full lifecycle of IT assets and software licenses: requirement gathering, annual budget planning, procurement, inventory record, maintenance, periodic audit and asset retirement;
7.  Administer core enterprise systems including AD, PBX, email platform, enterprise virtualisation platforms (e.g., Citrix) and NAS storage systems (e.g., Synology);
8.  Provide on-site support alongside the HQ network team; liaise with local network operators and exchanges, and handle office server rooms, network equipment and data centre issues;
9.  Develop technical documentation and operational SOPs to continuously standardise local IT workflows;
10.  Support the local IT compliance and security program: interpret regulatory requirements, implement information security controls, run risk assessments and security awareness training, and act as the local point of contact for regulators, external auditors and internal compliance on IT-related matters.

**Requirements**

1.  Able to prioritise workload autonomously, proactively identify IT risks and operational issues and drive resolutions with full ownership of outcomes;
2.  Solid project coordination skills to break down tasks, track progress and anticipate risks; escalate resource constraints or technical difficulties to HQ in a timely manner to ensure issue closure;
3.  Strong knowledge of PC hardware, Windows OS and macOS, application deployment & troubleshooting; proven experience in endpoint standardisation;
4.  Strong understanding of TCP/IP, DHCP, DNS; capable of resolving common network issues independently;
5.  Able to develop IT implementation plans with strong hands-on skills to execute hardware installation and system deployment following corporate standards;
6.  Practical experience in Windows Server, AD, email systems, PBX, virtualisation and NAS administration; MCSE, Microsoft 365 Certified, Azure Administrator or equivalent certifications are preferred;
7.  Business-fluent English for stakeholder communication and technical documentation writing; comfortable working across time zones and multicultural teams;
8.  Added advantages: knowledge of DRP/BCP operations; experience liaising with local regulators; direct experience in a securities firm or investment bank; familiarity with IT compliance programs (ISO 27001, SOC 2, PCI DSS or equivalent) and local data protection regulations (e.g. GDPR, PDPA) in a regulated financial services environment.

This local IT support role assists China HQ in rolling out global IT standards. You will deliver day-to-day IT support, equipment maintenance, basic network support and asset register management for office and retail stores.

### Key Responsibilities

* Assist in implementing corporate IT standards, policies and security controls; support project execution, data collection and corrective action implementation;
* Support IT infrastructure deployment for offices and retail sites, including site survey, hardware racking, cable management and basic system initialisation;
* Perform standardised PC deployment, software installation, routine maintenance and endpoint troubleshooting;
* Conduct regular inspection and maintenance for AV systems, access control, CCTV, IP phones and multi-function printers;
* Support administration of DNS and DHCP services; troubleshoot common network issues on user endpoints;
* Support full lifecycle IT asset management: maintain inventory records, goods receipt, stocktaking, maintenance follow-up and asset retirement documentation;
* Assist with daily monitoring, user permission administration support and routine checks on AD, email, NAS, virtualisation and PBX systems;
* Support HQ security and network teams with on-site activities; assist in communication with local regulators, external auditors and third-party vendors, and report on-site status and issues in a timely manner;
* Maintain operational logs, technical documents and SOPs to implement standardised local IT procedures.

**Requirements**

* Proactive and execution-oriented; follow defined procedures for daily IT tasks and report identified issues promptly;

* Able to prioritise daily support tickets; escalate unresolved issues in a timely manner to achieve proper closure;
* Practical knowledge of PC hardware, Windows OS and macOS, common office software; experience with OS reinstallation and endpoint troubleshooting;
* Basic understanding of TCP/IP, DHCP, DNS and capable of resolving typical office network faults;
* Hands-on IT skills to complete equipment installation and maintenance following standard operating procedures;
* Basic awareness of Windows Server, Active Directory, email, NAS and virtualisation; relevant working experience is a plus;
* Fluent in Arabic and English. Able to collaborate in a multicultural environment.

**Please note: Please note that only candidates selected for further consideration will receive a response.**

Hexagon Autonomous Solutions is seeking a highly skilled and detail-oriented a Project Engineer to be responsible for planning, coordinating, and executing technical projects to ensure they are delivered on time, within budget, and to the required quality standards. This role combines engineering expertise with project management skills, overseeing the full project lifecycle from design and implementation to testing and handover. Key responsibilities include developing project plans, managing resources, monitoring progress, mitigating risks, and ensuring compliance with safety and regulatory standards. Strong problem-solving, communication, and organisational skills are essential for success in this role
Scope of the Role:
The Hardware Technician will provide site-based and remote system support to the customer in the region. To deploy new and upgraded systems at customers mine sites. To do basic troubleshooting and configuration system software and computer operating systems. To develop procedures and system reports in response to the customer’s requests and needs.

• To have a strong and broad high-level knowledge of the mining systems deployed.

• To be a point of escalation for technical issues that the team raise as they are working on projects and to work through the escalation process to seek resolution to problems outside of the responsibility of the Project Engineers and other technical staff.

• To work with Project Managers to ensure the efficient deployment of mining systems on time and within budget.

• To ensure that the deployment of systems and products is carried out as efficiently as possible.

Key Responsibilities:

• The Hardware Technician is responsible and accountable for (but not limited to) the following:

• Defining and reviewing project proposals and plans with colleagues and customers

• Execution of projects including definition of project phases, elements and schedule;

• Determine project specifications by studying product design, customer requirements, performance standards;

• Prepare cost estimates;

• Loading of basic configurations, upgrades and operating systems onto computing; equipment (field and servers) following defined change management procedure;

• Maintain and control projects following standard project management standards including monitoring of project progress, coordinating activities, and problem resolution;

• Administer service agreements;

• Maintain project data base of deployed system and specific configurations;

• Writing computer programs, entering and backing up data;

• Contributes to team effort by accomplishing related results as and when required;

• Establish and maintain effective working relationships with Hardware Manager and Project Engineers;

• Quickly identify business risks, inefficiencies, issues and opportunities related to business applications;

• Monitor the market for new solutions and recommend solutions that will positively impact the project cycle.

• To ensure that all activities are carried out in accordance with the company’s Quality, Health, Safety & Environment (QHSE), Ethics & Compliance policies, etc.

• Working environment will vary from office to site based and can include working at heights and through challenging environmental conditions including heat, noise, and dust;

• Protect the company brand and reputation by exhibiting good behavior and reporting on any noncompliance to safety, procedural, or other customer dictated regulations;

• Maintain good relations with the customer ‘s personnel and clearly communicate any issues that may arise;

• Establish and maintain effective working relationships with managers, technicians and engineers;

• Continuously seek opportunities to improve the quality of the systems, installations, and support procedures;

Skill & Experience:
Experience with the application of technology in a harsh industrial environment;

• Good analytical skills to diagnose problems quickly and excellent customer service skills;

• Excellent communication skills and sensitive to varying levels of technical competency in clients and the pressures clients may be under while working with malfunctioning equipment;

• Experience of customer orientated environment;

• Knowledge of general network infrastructure and configuration and relevant technical experience;

• Ability to liaise with customers in an empathic and technically effective manner;

• Ability to work well within a team as well as on own;

• Documentation, Safety management and Microsoft Office tools;

• Comply with all health and safety measures in place on the customer’s mine sites;

• Clearly understand and comply with all the rules and regulations that exist on the customer’s mine sites and seek help if any confusion;

• Ensure that colleagues comply with health and safety regulations and address any irregularities;

• Maintain safe environment by enforcing procedures, rules, and regulations;

• Seek to identify and propose procedures that can improve health and safety in the workplace;

• Foster an environment that supports technical staff and allows them to succeed;

• The desire to expand own knowledge and skill set as well as sharing knowledge with other team members wherever possible.

• Ability to rapidly grasp technical solutions, concepts and products.

Key behaviour:

• Protect the company brand and reputation by exhibiting good behaviour and reporting on any noncompliance to safety, procedural, or other customer dictated regulations.

• Maintain good relations with the customer ‘s personnel and clearly communicate any issues that may arise.

• Establish and maintain effective working relationships with managers, technicians and engineers.

• Continuously seek opportunities to improve the quality of the systems, installations, and support procedures.

Educational Background:

• N6 with trade test, National diploma, bachelor’s degree or foreign degree equivalent in Engineering (Computer / Mining / Electrical /Electronic/Mechanical), or a related field.

• A minimum of 2 years of experience in previous Mining Industry experience of progressive experience in job offered, or as a hardware installation and maintenance technician, or related occupational title.

• Fluency in English. French is an added advantage.

• Previous experience working remote teams (Highly Desirable)

Travel:

• Flexible as the successful candidate would be required to sometimes work on weekends, and travel to different sites with many being outside of the country.

• Candidate must have a current Passport and valid driver’s license, as well as pass a background check.

